   "ref": "main",
   "sha": "a81d6fd7c516f70706f7cfe200c90a98892e8199"
  },
  "body": "Fixes #339946\n\n## Summary\n\nWhen screen readers (such as VoiceOver on macOS) navigate through items in an `ActionList` (e.g. the branch picker in the Agents window), the codicon font glyph elements in the DOM were not hidden from assistive technology. This resulted in VoiceOver announcing an unrenderable font character (represented as a question mark gremlin glyph `[?]`) before items.\n\n## Fix\n- Added `ariaHidden = 'true'` to the `icon` element in `ActionItemRenderer.renderTemplate` (consistent with badges).\n- Added `ariaHidden = 'true'` to the `submenuIndicator` element.\n- Added a unit test in `actionList.test.ts` verifying `aria-hidden=\"true\"` on both elements.",
  "rebaseable": true
 },
